1. Why should each cost component be stored in a separate variable instead of one long expression?
So that it can be easily read and debugged when a problem occurs. 
2. If passengers were stored as a double instead of an int, would the final numerical result change?
No, it will not change the numerical result, but it is more appropriate to store it as an int because you do not need a decimal when counting passengers. 
3. What output-formatting feature makes the fare breakdown easier to verify?
When it is formatted with a decimal point set to 2 places to represent centavos. 
